.TH KISA-CCE-POLICY-COMPILE 8 "2026-09-04" "KISA CCE Linux Scanner" "System Administration Commands"
.SH NAME
kisa-cce-policy-compile \- compile policy YAML into scanner policy TSV
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kisa-cce-policy-compile
.BI \-\-input " FILE"
.BI \-\-output-dir " PATH"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kisa-cce-policy-compile
converts an author-friendly, policy-specific YAML subset into the strict TSV
directory consumed by
.BR kisa-cce-scan (8).
The scanner itself does not parse YAML.
.PP
The compiler uses no YAML library and does not implement general YAML.  It
accepts only schema version 1, block lists with fixed mappings, full-line
comments, plain scalars, and quoted scalars with a restricted escape set.
Anchors, aliases, tags, merge keys, flow collections, block scalars, multiple
documents, tabs, carriage returns, and inline comments in plain scalars are
rejected.  ASCII and Unicode C1 control characters and malformed UTF-8 are
also rejected.
.PP
After conversion, the compiler reloads the generated directory through the
scanner's canonical policy validator.  Invalid criterion codes, decisions,
review IDs, dates, providers, source identities, duplicates, or expired-field
syntax therefore fail before publication.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-input " FILE"
Read the policy YAML from
.IR FILE .
The path may be relative to the current directory.  The input must be a
readable regular file owned by root or the effective user, with no group or
other write permission.  Symbolic links and untrusted parent paths are
rejected.
.TP
.BI \-\-output-dir " PATH"
Create a new compiled policy directory at
.IR PATH .
The target must not already exist.  The parent must be a trusted physical
directory.  Existing paths are never overwritten.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print command help and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the scanner version and policy YAML schema version, then exit.
.SH YAML SCHEMA
The document must begin with the schema declaration and an attestation list:
.PP
.EX
schema_version: 1
attestations:
  - code: U-64
    decision: GOOD
    review_id: sha256:0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef
    ticket: SEC-2026-0142
    approver: security-governance
    expires: 2026-12-31
.EE
.PP
.B attestations
is required and may be the explicit empty list
.BR [] .
The optional
.B time_sources
list uses provider, host, address, ticket, approver, and expires fields.
Omitting it leaves the typed fact set absent.  Writing
.B "time_sources: []"
creates an explicit empty approved-source set and is therefore a policy
decision rather than a neutral placeholder.
.PP
Mapping field order is unrestricted.  Every required field must occur exactly
once.  List markers use two spaces of indentation, and continuation fields use
four.  Full-line comments and blank lines are accepted.  Plain values that are
ambiguous under the restricted grammar must be single- or double-quoted.
Within double quotes, only an escaped double quote or backslash is accepted.
Within single quotes, one quote is represented by two consecutive quotes.
.SH OUTPUT
On success, the compiler creates an owner-only directory containing
.I 50-compiled.tsv
and, when
.B time_sources
was supplied,
.IR facts/time-sources.tsv .
Directories use mode 0700 and files use mode 0600.
.PP
Every terminal line uses the dmesg-style scanner prefix.  Success prints:
.PP
.EX
[    12.345678] kisa-cce-policy-compile: policy_directory=/absolute/path
[    12.345678] kisa-cce-policy-compile: policy_digest=sha256:HEX_DIGEST
.EE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The generated policy directory passed structural and canonical validation.
.TP
.B 2
Invocation, path validation, YAML parsing, policy validation, or publication
failed.  No completed output directory is reported.
.SH SECURITY
The wrapper clears the caller environment before loading Bash code.  YAML is
parsed as data and is never sourced or evaluated.  Input and output directories
are pinned by file descriptors, and publication uses a no-replace rename in the
target parent.
.PP
Compilation does not authorize a policy decision.  Review IDs, tickets,
approvers, and expiration dates remain administrative security inputs.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/kisa-cce-scanner/policy.d/
Default installed policy directory consumed by complete and automation scans.
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/kisa-cce-linux-scanner/examples/policy.yml
Possible package documentation location for the source example.  The upstream
.B make install
target does not install repository documentation or examples.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kisa-cce-scan (8)
